{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma","id":1263386,"title":"Help with Steal Devil MA","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-10-29T10:40:46-07:00","id":1263386,"title":"Help with Steal Devil MA","content":"Im planning on using the Steal Devil MA, but im not sure how the charms should be used.<br /> Could you share with me some tips, advice and experiences that you had in play with the style?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11395-shaddar","name":"Shaddar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"338"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T12:12:50-07:00","id":1263399,"title":"","content":"Our Night Caste uses it a bit. It seemed that Double-Attack Technique doesn't really increase damage much against high-defence foes (it can even reduce damage) unless you've built up good off-hand charge, so be careful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T12:53:27-07:00","id":1263407,"title":"","content":"Hmm. How would it reduce damage against high defense foes? Double Attack has no conditional damage other than &quot;beat his defense again to gain this extra damage&quot;<br /> (for a non-terrestrial like your night caste)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 10-29-2018, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T13:23:03-07:00","id":1263411,"title":"","content":"Because you get it instead of the threshold successes.<br /> <br /> For example, if you're attacking someone with Defence 6, and you get 7 successes to hit, the charm doesn't do anything.<br /> <br /> If you get 12 successes, the charm triggers, and you do -2 Overwhelming instead of -1, and you do the charm's damage instead of those 6 threshold successes. So, if you have Dex 4 and 3 points of Offhand Charge, instead of doing 6 damage for 6 threshold successes, you'll do the charm's damage bonus, in this case +5. You might want to use it anyway, because of the better Overwhelming Penalty, but it's worth bearing in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-29-2018, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T13:49:58-07:00","id":1263413,"title":"","content":"Almost. You still get threshold successes that weren't necessary to make the second hit. So against 6 defense a 12 successes double attack would hit at 6, and then hit at 5, leaving 1 threshold to add to damage.<br /> Still, dex + half charge, which you can count to start with 2. A terrestrial will start with a 3, others can expect 4s and 5s and 6s.<br /> <br /> Well, fits the overall design of &quot;you don't want to use this against someone immune to onslaught&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T15:17:43-07:00","id":1263426,"title":"","content":"Honestly all Steel Devil Style is a weird one in that all the pre-form charms are pretty bad but all the post-form ones are crazy strong/borderline op. So basically pay the charm tax, don't waste your motes on Double Attack Technique and spam those Sonic Slashes like there's no tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T17:07:21-07:00","id":1263439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shaddar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma#post1263386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you share with me some tips, advice and experiences that you had in play with the style?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't use Steel Devil. Currently the worst MA in the entire game. The only thing it excels in is beating people weaker than you, Single Point is laughably better than it in every way. Shit White Reaper is better than it.<br /> <br /> You're better off just taking melee and making duel wielding charms.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T20:12:40-07:00","id":1263473,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't despair, I desperately need sleep right now so I can't post more than a few sentences until tomorrow, but Steel Devil can be great, you just need to know what you're getting yourself into and how to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T20:54:18-07:00","id":1263482,"title":"","content":"I ran some test duels last year for my pseudo-Infernal to see whether Steel Devil or Solar Melee would be better as his primary offensive mode. 5 charms into each, they were ultimately about as effective; he won all but one of the fights I ran (the sole loss being against the Core's sample Deathknight using Melee). Melee strikes me as being more potentially powerful in the long run\u2014not to mention more versatile\u2014but at chargen Steel Devil is a viable alternative if the style appeals to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T09:36:45-07:00","id":1263601,"title":"","content":"Had to do some digging, but back in May <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2746_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2746\" data-vbnamecard=\"2746\">TGUEIROS</a> actually did a pretty good analysis of Steel Devil beyond what I had always heard of it being a &quot;win moar&quot; style.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1215880-i-know-kung-fu-or-let-s-talk-about-martial-arts?p=1216292#post1216292\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1215880-i-know-kung-fu-or-let-s-talk-about-martial-arts?p=1216292#post1216292\"> I know kung fu (OR Let's talk about martial arts!) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1215880-i-know-kung-fu-or-let-s-talk-about-martial-arts?p=1216292#post1216292\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1215880-i-know-kung-fu-or-let-s-talk-about-martial-arts?p=1216292#post1216292 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Put simply, this thread is for a discussion of all things martial arts in Exalted. Which are your favorite styles? Your favorite MA charms? Your favorite MA combos? Which styles pair best? What works and what doesn't work? Best practices for building and playing a martial artist? Let's leave discussion of interaction with non-MA charms (Solar, DB, etc.) to another thread; this thread is for the love of MA. Challenge: your exalt isn't really a martial artist until she knows the form charms of at least two styles and has reflexively switched from one to the other in a battle. Come at me, bro. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T10:08:45-07:00","id":1263609,"title":"","content":"Interesting point about combining Double-Attack/Triple-Attack with Fire Dragon Form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T10:15:25-07:00","id":1263615,"title":"","content":"TL;DR on Steel Devil is that it is absolutely NOT for soloing with. You want to make it work, you do so by letting your allies stack some onslaught penalties on your target first, because their Defense essentially counts for double against your main trick. If you can make it past that hurdle though and are willing to blow all your Willpower in a round or two, your enemies <i>will</i> blend (Wyld Hunt smoke, don\u2019t breathe this!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 10-30-2018, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T10:21:11-07:00","id":1263620,"title":"","content":"Plus, you yourself are stacking a good amount of Overwhelming for your allies to take advantage of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T11:26:04-07:00","id":1263631,"title":"","content":"Yeah Steel Devil gets meme'd as more useless than it actually is, but <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10131_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10131\" data-vbnamecard=\"10131\">BadassOverlord</a> has it right: as far as I'm concerned, the entire style may be hot garbage and it would still be worth it for the ability to get up to +5 autosuxx on rushes for 4m (Seconds Between Strife), what's basically for all intents and purposes a perfect defense without a reset condition for 3m (Twin-Blade Defense), and the ability to make decisives without using up your initiative. Hell, at higher Essence, even Naked Fang Draw becomes a twice as mote-effective Join Battle enhancer as the Awareness excellency, without requiring any kind of investment on your part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T12:03:10-07:00","id":1263641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1263601#post1263601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had to do some digging, but back in May <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> actually did a pretty good analysis of Steel Devil beyond what I had always heard of it being a &amp;quot;win moar&amp;quot; style.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1215880-i-know-kung-fu-or-let-s-talk-about-martial-arts?p=1216292#post1216292\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...92#post1216292</a></div> </div> </div> </div>This is my issue with it. It's too easily shut down by onslaught negators. Tiger style likes low defense but it isn't completely reliant on it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sandact stop being paranoid. Not everyone has onslaught negators much less solar ones.&quot;<br /> <br /> True not everyone does, but the very second you run into someone who can then you're knee capped. Tiger has lots of stuff you can do on high defense. Ebon shadow has lots of things you can do outside of stealth. The only things steel devil has is the fairly good defense charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T12:06:12-07:00","id":1263642,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... Seconds Between Strife is good, but I don't think it's utterly amazing. You need to risk your charge, and the 4m cost could have given you +4 dice from your Athletics excellency anyway. <br /> (Obviously if you don't have an Athletics excellency, that's different.)<br /> <br /> Twin-Blade Defence is extremely good though, I agree.<br /> And at Essence 5, yeah, Naked Fang Draw is very good. Plus, it saves anyone who doesn't favour Awareness from having to spend 10xp to get Sensory Acuity Prana just to get the Awareness excellency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T12:30:50-07:00","id":1263651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1263641#post1263641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is my issue with it. It's too easily shut down by onslaught negators. Tiger style likes low defense but it isn't completely reliant on it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sandact stop being paranoid. Not everyone has onslaught negators much less solar ones.&quot;<br /> <br /> True not everyone does, but the very second you run into someone who can then you're knee capped. Tiger has lots of stuff you can do on high defense. Ebon shadow has lots of things you can do outside of stealth. The only things steel devil has is the fairly good defense charms.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't disagree; I just wanted to share the detailed breakdown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T15:05:00-07:00","id":1263674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1263601#post1263601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Had to do some digging, but back in May <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2746_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2746\" data-vbnamecard=\"2746\">TGUEIROS</a> actually did a pretty good analysis of Steel Devil beyond what I had always heard of it being a &quot;win moar&quot; style.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1215880-i-know-kung-fu-or-let-s-talk-about-martial-arts?p=1216292#post1216292\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...92#post1216292</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to add a few things to that post actually, hopefully without going over the same material too much. There's a few points that I'll take a look at.<br /> <br /> <b>Steel Devil is For Beating Opponents That You'd Beat Anyway</b><br /> <br /> Yes, that's true, that's one of the things it's good at, but that's not a bad thing. Let's say you're facing a foe with 4 defense and you've got an attack of 20 dice with a stunt and two motes using short daiklaves. Then you spend 3 motes into Triple Attack Technique putting you equal with your per round regen. You're doing 10 + (Strength) + (Dex) + (Charge) + (essence) + Overflow damage with that attack. With Naked Fang Draw it's not hard to start a fight with a full bar of charge, and assuming strength 3 that's a damage of +24 + (essence)*, with a light weapon. For 5 motes. 2 of which are boosting accuracy to help you hit anyway. If you're in Steel Devil Form it gets even cheaper.<br /> <br /> So why does that matter if you were going to win anyway? Firstly, if you're facing off against a big bad guy and a few of his lesser mook guys, then you've just driven one of them into the ground and gotten some crazy initiative off them while barely trying. Secondly though, even for fights that don't have a big bad guy right there, winning with little effort matters. For one if you're in a dodgy area not flaring your anima is great. For another your ally, who's using melee and blows half his mote pool crushing lesser, foes will be much less prepared for the final big boss. Lastly, although this matters somewhat less due to how badass most PCs are, even little enemies can be dangerous if you don't deal with them quickly. If you are trying to save motes and not flare, then that means greater risk.<br /> <br /> <b>Steel Devil is For Group Fights Not Solo</b><br /> <br /> I wouldn't necessarily say that, allow me to suggest a stragegy. Absolutely agree with the other posters here that Steel Devil loves fighting in groups, either to apply an onslaught penalty for her allies, or greatly benefitting off it herself. If one of your allies MAKES your opponent have 3 defense, well that's just grand. On the other hand though, even in a duel, or a duel style portion of a larger fight, you have options, and one of them is to use an initiative flip like melee does with One Weapon Two Blows. If your opponent starts with higher initiative than you, which isn't hard since you dump all yours into Charge off Join Battle, and you attack them, sending them below you in initiative, then before their defense resets you get to attack again. This will allow you to onslaught with yourself, no allies needed.<br /> <br /> What would be nice, if you could, is to go absolutely all out, and try to get at least a double attack technique on the first hit, if you can do that, you've won. It's not so bad, Exalted favours attacking over defending, especially with light weapons. Going all out you've got an attack pool of 28 with a stunt, and up to 3 more auto successes from better stunts and willpower. This isn't really helpful against a Solar who's likewise going all out on defense. You'll never get a double attack off on them, sadly.<br /> <br /> If you're fighting somebody who's got like 7-8 defense though, that's actually doable. If it DOES happen, and you proceed to launch a Steel Devil Strike afterwards, then you've just lowered his initiative to lower than yours, given a -3 onslaught penalty, and done some damage. Then you get to go again, and his defense is at 4-5 to start out with. Go all out again for a triple attack technique and their defense will be down to ~0. That in turn lets you do your Steel Devil Strike into an Empty Mind Strike into a Dervish Blade Frenzy, into another one of the former. At this point their defense is so low you don't need to spend any motes on hitting. Which is good because all those charms cost motes and willpower, something you'll be out of afterwards.<br /> <br /> <b>When it doesn't work, it sucks</b><br /> <br /> The above tactic also doesn't work on any Solar who's taken Bulwark Stance for themselves, obviously. It also combos well enough with Fire Dragon to get boosts to every attack in that second flurry that I outlined above, but that doesn't help if you can't get it off. This is going to be kind of campaign dependent, if your ST never throws enemies at you with less than 9-10 defense, you're just not going to have a good time. There's a few tricks you can still use like Cross-Blade Catch into Iron Lotus Unfurling, and Seconds Before Strife into Sonic Slash, but your main gimmick is hamstringed.<br /> <br /> You can look at this one of two ways. Well, assuming your campaign isn't just fighting Dawns, in which case you should look the way of another MA. First, you could just diversify your martial arts. Steel Devil can share form weapons with Snake, Single Point, Fire Dragon, and debatably Crane. All of these styles have ways to shore up your defenses against the kinds of targets you're bad at fighting, or in some cases apply a defense penalty that you can then take advantage of with Steel Devil.<br /> <br /> The other tactic is just to understand that your Steel Devil Style is not great at what it's not great at, and console yourself with the fact that no other style is as efficient at doing what you do either. Also, personally, I find that fights that don't involve the entire group are really rare, most STs like to avoid them because it usually sucks for the players not involved. So really it's just how often you run into dudes with casual onslaught negators.<br /> <br /> <br /> *I'm counting Triple Attack's &quot;damage rerolls&quot; here as just bonus damage, because for pools that big it basically is.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: After a clarification by Vance Triple Attack Technique is not nearly as good as I thought it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 10-31-2018, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T16:07:08-07:00","id":1263688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1263439#post1263439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't use Steel Devil. Currently the worst MA in the entire game. The only thing it excels in is beating people weaker than you, Single Point is laughably better than it in every way. Shit White Reaper is better than it.<br /> <br /> You're better off just taking melee and making duel wielding charms.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At risk of derrailing the thread, why &quot;Shit White Reaper is better than it.&quot;?<br /> Is there a problem with white reaper?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11395-shaddar","name":"Shaddar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"338"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T16:32:07-07:00","id":1263693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shaddar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1263688#post1263688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> At risk of derrailing the thread, why &quot;Shit White Reaper is better than it.&quot;?<br /> Is there a problem with white reaper?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to speak for Sandact6, but I would wager it's a combination of White Reaper's focus on fighting battlegroups, something that doesn't come up that often and equally often isn't that difficult to deal with, and it's halo mechanic. The mechanic, if you've not got a battlegroup handy, can be difficult to build halos for, and don't give the the most world-ending effects once you do build up 2-3 of them. Also many of the charms that use the halos burn them up, which isn't so good when you had to work so hard to get them in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T17:19:18-07:00","id":1263699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1263642#post1263642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... Seconds Between Strife is good, but I don't think it's utterly amazing. You need to risk your charge, and the 4m cost could have given you +4 dice from your Athletics excellency anyway.<br /> (Obviously if you don't have an Athletics excellency, that's different.)<br /> <br /> Twin-Blade Defence is extremely good though, I agree.<br /> And at Essence 5, yeah, Naked Fang Draw is very good. Plus, it saves anyone who doesn't favour Awareness from having to spend 10xp to get Sensory Acuity Prana just to get the Awareness excellency.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK yea I forgot about the Rush charm after I posted (Lunch was over and I needed to get back to work). The rush charm, as mentioned, is also legit amazing.<br /> <br /> Naked Fang Strike, for reasons mentioned, is also amazing. Its just that firing it off is completely luck based.<br /> <br /> In fact I think one of the most damning things about Steel Devil is that it goes from being bottom tier of the Martial Arts pile to near the top <i>in a single artifact</i> (Dawn's Fangs, refluffed as shortswords) is pretty damn telling. I mean sure hitting an enemy with 0 defense is bad for them, but when you fire off Triple Attack Technique on them? Oh shit.<br /> <br /> Also the later stages of the style are incredibly expensive. They're powerful yes, but I don't think that they're worth the cost.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoroseMorgan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1263651#post1263651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't disagree; I just wanted to share the detailed breakdown.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was mainly attempting to counter such arguments, as I've heard them come up before. Hell even if you run into something that can HALF Defense penalties you're still more than screwed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shaddar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1263688#post1263688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> At risk of derrailing the thread, why &quot;Shit White Reaper is better than it.&quot;?<br /> Is there a problem with white reaper?</div> </div> </div> </div>White Reaper excels at fighting battle groups or multiple opponents. It excels at doing so and honestly when outnumber the power on it climbs to enormous heights.<br /> <br /> But in 1v1 duels? Its hard to get off the ground. The beginning two charms are good, but really hard to work up halos when you are reliant on crashing opponents. If you have other methods to generate them then it can spike up.<br /> <br /> And I don't mind &quot;Oh its useless compared to Single Point&quot;. Single Point and Righteous Devil are the strongest MA's in the game (I'd say Devil is a hair away from being broken) but even when you compare it to other martial arts the differences become clear pretty quickly. I mean Earth Dragon without Aura benefits is way better than White Reaper at single targets, but against battle groups and multiple opponents White Reaper is better.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T17:31:34-07:00","id":1263704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1263699#post1263699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I don't mind &quot;Oh its useless compared to Single Point&quot;. Single Point and Righteous Devil are the strongest MA's in the game (I'd say Devil is a hair away from being broken)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh really? I haven't really looked into it, what's so broken about RD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T19:18:28-07:00","id":1263726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1263704#post1263704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh really? I haven't really looked into it, what's so broken about RD?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Getting dual 5 shooters for the style pretty much removes the need to reload for most combats. I've rarely seen combat go above 3 turns.<br /> <br /> 2) The form applies aim actions on targets, making it so that you can fire out to medium range every turn without aiming. Yes it has an activation condition to go with it, but the dicepool for doing so is generous. Firewands are short, but the moment you find a way around this the style explodes. Firewand evocations have to be very careful with range extensions as a result.<br /> <br /> 3) Because you're aiming on someone always, Kiss of the Sun gives +3 automatic damage every turn as a Solar. Phoenix Flies on Golden Wings is also efficient to the point of insanity, giving additional automatic successes on damage. Total both of those for extremely punishing withering attacks combined with the form means you're not missing often.<br /> <br /> 4) Dancing Devil Trigger Finger + Caress of 1000 Hells = Pretty much instant encounter ended if you go with the rule of &quot;AoE attacks need only to supplement one attack&quot;. Single point may do more damage in a single hit, but if Righteous Devil allows this combination you can snap entire encounters in half.<br /> <br /> I am aware Vance said that the MA's were designed a long time ago. A time when Hungry Tiger Technique only cost 2m and could be used regardless of opponent status. Many of them were not updated to match the current balance of the game and that needs to factor into how people evaluate them and other MA's in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T20:16:55-07:00","id":1263733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1263726#post1263726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am aware Vance said that the MA's were designed a long time ago. A time when Hungry Tiger Technique only cost 2m and could be used regardless of opponent status. Many of them were not updated to match the current balance of the game and that needs to factor into how people evaluate them and other MA's in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, THAT'S interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T21:59:33-07:00","id":1263740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1263726#post1263726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Getting dual 5 shooters</div> </div> </div> </div>As in revolvers, which don\u2019t exist? Or does this mean something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T22:52:14-07:00","id":1263746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1263726#post1263726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) Getting dual 5 shooters for the style pretty much removes the need to reload for most combats. I've rarely seen combat go above 3 turns.<br /> <br /> 2) The form applies aim actions on targets, making it so that you can fire out to medium range every turn without aiming. Yes it has an activation condition to go with it, but the dicepool for doing so is generous. Firewands are short, but the moment you find a way around this the style explodes. Firewand evocations have to be very careful with range extensions as a result.<br /> <br /> 3) Because you're aiming on someone always, Kiss of the Sun gives +3 automatic damage every turn as a Solar. Phoenix Flies on Golden Wings is also efficient to the point of insanity, giving additional automatic successes on damage. Total both of those for extremely punishing withering attacks combined with the form means you're not missing often.<br /> <br /> 4) Dancing Devil Trigger Finger + Caress of 1000 Hells = Pretty much instant encounter ended if you go with the rule of &quot;AoE attacks need only to supplement one attack&quot;. Single point may do more damage in a single hit, but if Righteous Devil allows this combination you can snap entire encounters in half.<br /> <br /> I am aware Vance said that the MA's were designed a long time ago. A time when Hungry Tiger Technique only cost 2m and could be used regardless of opponent status. Many of them were not updated to match the current balance of the game and that needs to factor into how people evaluate them and other MA's in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>As near as I can tell, Exalted 3e doesn't have any kind of revolvers in it.<br /> <br /> Dancing Devil Trigger Finger only hits up to three targets and they have to be at medium range and positioned properly. Now, it looks like that should work with Caress of 1000 Hells, but applying that charm to three people doesn't necessarily seem like it'll break an encounter in half. Especially since it's an expensive trick that can only be used once per scene, so if there are more than three dangerous opponents or if they flank you, you might be in trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T23:48:36-07:00","id":1263751,"title":"","content":"I will point out that while Revolvers don't exist, Sirrush and Sekhem both let you reload reflexively (though it's not cheap).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T05:38:08-07:00","id":1263765,"title":"","content":"Really? People are forgetting the Flametongue Repeater are a thing? The one that very clearly says it has 5 shots?<br /> <br /> Pretty much all games I've been in (Or watched/heard of) where players get Righteous Devil they attempt to beeline for these weapons immediately.<br /> <br /> Before you say homebrew, not really. They're one of the weapons cut from the leak. Sirrush might just be that one as its renamed &quot;Devil Caster&quot; instead. We don't know as it lacks any kind of description for it. Even if you homebrew it instead its very piss easy to reverse engineer it from 2.Xe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1263746#post1263746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dancing Devil Trigger Finger only hits up to three targets and they have to be at medium range and positioned properly. Now, it looks like that should work with Caress of 1000 Hells, but applying that charm to three people doesn't necessarily seem like it'll break an encounter in half. Especially since it's an expensive trick that can only be used once per scene, so if there are more than three dangerous opponents or if they flank you, you might be in trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Combats are assumed to start at Short range (or just have an ally tie people up for you) then get to a range where you can hit the maximum number of people.<br /> <br /> 2) Dancing Devil Trigger Finger + Blossom of Demise + Kiss of the Sun Concentration + Phoenix Flies on Golden Wings + 1000 Hells. What we have is a combo that adds minimum 5 additional damage dice at Medium with an attack that before you <b>against multiple enemies which allows you to use your full initiative</b> (Compared to other multi attacks in the game which split it), if you pulled the form off right, is getting +3 non charm dice to attack everyone in the area.<br /> <br /> 3) But that damage is really irrelevant. Because if 1000 Hells hit then everyone does either repents and gets a Major intimacy right away (Pretty powerful) and automatically crashes if they attempt to fight back. If they continue fighting anyways they take (Essence) aggravated <b>levels</b> of damage and take an equal penalty for the rest of the encounter equal to the damage. Nearly no one is going to recover from that penalty.<br /> <br /> You could say it takes time to set up, but if pulled off the encounter is effectively over or opponents are booted in the balls. This isn't some sort of charop thing which requires all the planets to be aligned, it just requires some opponents at least in the same zone. If you nail four enemies at least then that's often an entire encounter.<br /> <br /> Its a pretty fair assumption that you can force using supplemental charms once per each opponent in blast or use the 2.5e rules for Strafing/automatic fire (Supplemental charms are tripled in price), but even if you do such things the martial art is still incredibly powerful. Adding so much dice on damage, stupidly powerful AoE, and auto-aiming capabilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":1183,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","user":"Sandact6","date":". 10-31-2018, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T06:23:52-07:00","id":1263774,"title":"","content":"The Flametongue Repeater may have been cut because it's OP when combined with Righteous Devil. I thought it was notable that the artefact weapons in Arms included the Devil Caster, not the Flametongue Repeater (not that reloading Sirrush is exactly hard!).<br /> <br /> Not arguing with your other points though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T07:05:57-07:00","id":1263785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1263774#post1263774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Flametongue Repeater may have been cut because it's OP when combined with Righteous Devil. I thought it was notable that the artefact weapons in Arms included the Devil Caster, not the Flametongue Repeater (not that reloading Sirrush is exactly hard!).<br /> <br /> Not arguing with your other points though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't stop people attempting to get one ASAP. It won't until we have official word too.<br /> <br /> TBH it was only broken with Righteous Devil. With archery it's fine. If Righteous Devil could only attack every other turn then the damage would even out. But that makes it s bit more boring to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T13:14:27-07:00","id":1263865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1263699#post1263699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact I think one of the most damning things about Steel Devil is that it goes from being bottom tier of the Martial Arts pile to near the top <i>in a single artifact</i> (Dawn's Fangs, refluffed as shortswords) is pretty damn telling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are they found? I don't recognize the name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/513-gatts","name":"Gatts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T13:40:55-07:00","id":1263871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gatts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1263865#post1263865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are they found? I don't recognize the name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the first draft that got cut. It was a pair of Tiger Claws with powerful but confusing as fuck Evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T14:51:49-07:00","id":1263897,"title":"","content":"I feel like, if you're using material that was cut from the game with certain martial arts and are finding the results amazingly powerful, it might not be the martial arts that are the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T15:34:15-07:00","id":1263905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1263897#post1263897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like, if you're using material that was cut from the game with certain martial arts and are finding the results amazingly powerful, it might not be the martial arts that are the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reskinning tiger claws as repeating flame pieces especially. You need to be careful with exalted, doing so much as reskinning a knife as a sword can have bad consequences. Of course some stuff doesn\u2019t even need a rules tweak to get silly but you don\u2019t need to be adding to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T15:58:06-07:00","id":1263916,"title":"","content":"I think that, generally speaking, reskinning evocation trees isn't a big problem; Nightmare Cutter works fine as a Daiklaive, but Vance realised there was already a bunch of daiklaives (including 2 moonsilver) and no artefact boomerangs, so it ended up being a Sky-Cutter, rather than a daiklaive. I don't think anything in the evocation tree is broken on a medium melee weapon.<br /> <br /> But the exception is when they combine with MA. Certainly MAs are designed with compatibility or lack thereof in mind; I think the evocation trees for weapons somewhat consider what MAs they are compatible with. (The same applies for Brawl/Melee; I notice none of the Brawl weapons have much in the way of defensive evocations, which maintains the key weakness of the Brawl tree.)<br /> <br /> Plus, when we talk about evocation trees that were cut from the Core; well, the evocation trees in the Core were changed substantially before publication. They weren't just cut for word-count. Obviously John and Holden felt they weren't good for the game; perhaps some of them were overpowered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-31-2018, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T17:24:39-07:00","id":1263939,"title":"","content":"Evocations changed because they were bloated as hell. John and Morke had another system planned for Evocations but were fired and pulled all their material (Morke claiming that his Stormcaller was so much better as he spent over 100 XP on its stuff).<br /> <br /> Its also not the stats that matter when it come to Dawn's Fangs, more of the tags. Swords have the Melee tag. Do you want to give Melee access to Falling Hammer Strike? Tiger Claws have the Brawl tag, so they're not as bad there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1263897#post1263897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like, if you're using material that was cut from the game with certain martial arts and are finding the results amazingly powerful, it might not be the martial arts that are the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>No I think its more of a case if one particular thing makes something hideously broken? It might be good to have a look at both. Remember the Adamant Skin Gemstone with Laughing Wounds? Fun times. The difference here is that rather than breaking the game over its knee it makes one Martial Art go from weakest in the game to one of the strongest. Literally no other martial art gets that kind of power boost, the only one that comes close is Tiger and not nearly as much. I mention the Dawn's Fangs because thematically they also match Steel Devil's style too, both in fluff and in crunch. A person who wants to use them could make a case to their ST and not sound crazy like wanting to make Stormcaller into claws.<br /> <br /> The same can be said of Righteous Devil. It has the opposite problem in that its crazy strong, the five shooter just makes it stronger. Or hell just use Sirrush as a template for an idea and you have a 1m automatic reloading action. 1m per shot is hen's feed. Or you know literally everyone ever wanting to replicate their cowboy aspect and going really hard for six/five shooters the second they realize that is a thing.<br /> <br /> No if one item makes an entire style break in two I think you should start with the style itself.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-31T23:14:41-07:00","id":1263985,"title":"","content":"I have to say looking back over it, it definitely feels like RD style is balanced for only making an attack every other turn. Even at firing every other turn it's very powerful. I also have to admit that expecting players not to want a revolver of some kind as a special artifact seems...off somehow. On the other hand I have absolutely no idea how to fix that without being punishing. Maybe I'm just too used to DB level charms recently.<br /> <br /> On the other hand with the terrestrial keywords it's better, and I've sort of given up trying to balance things for Solars. At least with my players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T02:30:55-07:00","id":1263997,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it seems much weaker for Dragonblood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T06:02:47-07:00","id":1264016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1263997#post1263997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it seems much weaker for Dragonblood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, okay, stating the obvious, I know. Actually that maybe a cool way to have a DB in a Solar party, give them a revolver style artifact flame piece and let them go crazy with RD. Starting at essence 2 means they can grab Phoenix Flies on Golden Wings and Azure Abacus right off the hop. It should level the playing field a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T06:33:27-07:00","id":1264021,"title":"","content":"Or Sekhem. It's resonant for them, and they can fire it every round for some motes (4 in the first round, 3 in the second, 2 in the third, etc), with its higher damage.<br /> <br /> Or Sirrush (which lets you fire every round by reloading reflexively), but I think Sekhem is more powerful, personally. I guess Sirrush is more, hmmm, flexible? Giving you anti-surprise charms and knocking people over and stuff, whereas Sekhem is more just about doing lots of damage.<br /> <br /> DBs can of course also reload firewands reflexively using Archery charms (for 2m, 1i), but those probably aren't as powerful as Righteous Devil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T07:22:23-07:00","id":1264030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1264021#post1264021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Sekhem. It's resonant for them, and they can fire it every round for some motes (4 in the first round, 3 in the second, 2 in the third, etc), with its higher damage.<br /> <br /> Or Sirrush (which lets you fire every round by reloading reflexively), but I think Sekhem is more powerful, personally. I guess Sirrush is more, hmmm, flexible? Giving you anti-surprise charms and knocking people over and stuff, whereas Sekhem is more just about doing lots of damage.<br /> <br /> DBs can of course also reload firewands reflexively using Archery charms (for 2m, 1i), but those probably aren't as powerful as Righteous Devil.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can reload with an archery charm and then fire with RD though, right? 2m1i isn\u2019t that expensive, and with the smaller more pools I might not find it a bad trade off to pay it twice, rather than the 7 motes for Sekhem twice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T07:35:32-07:00","id":1264031,"title":"","content":"You can, though it requires 2 charms and Archery 4.<br /> <br /> Whereas Sirrush includes the reload charm for free when you attune it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 11-01-2018, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T07:39:06-07:00","id":1264033,"title":"","content":"Ah good point there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T22:46:28-07:00","id":1264210,"title":"","content":"At worst one can always flurry the reload.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-02T06:10:15-07:00","id":1264255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1264210#post1264210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At worst one can always flurry the reload.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, right, duh. I\u2019ve never had a player in my game use a flame piece before. It\u2019s also been a year and a half since I played 3e so that\u2019s probably not helping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-02T06:37:28-07:00","id":1264258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1264255#post1264255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, right, duh. I\u2019ve never had a player in my game use a flame piece before. It\u2019s also been a year and a half since I played 3e so that\u2019s probably not helping.</div> </div> </div> </div>It still privies the character from its simple charms, as well as imposing a penalty. So there's that XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-02T06:52:11-07:00","id":1264261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1263985#post1263985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say looking back over it, it definitely feels like RD style is balanced for only making an attack every other turn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait what - no, it isn't.<br /> <br /> Cloud of Ebon Devils literally says &quot;whenever the stylist aims with a firewand, she may also reload it&quot;. It specifically says &quot;aims&quot;, rather than &quot;uses his action to aim&quot;. Guess what the Form Charm gives you? Free reflexive aims against characters you've successfully influenced at its activation (or later social actions). This is one of the most basic ways the style's effects combo together, I can't believe that the entire thread missed this.<br /> <br /> Back on topic: the reason why I feel that it's pointless to worry about how easy it is to counter Steel Devil's shtick is that in Ex3, <i>basically any build can be countered</i>. If your GM wants you to have a difficult time, you will have a difficult time. If they want to give you an easy win that plays to your style's strengths, you will get an easy win that plays to your style's strengths. A comprehensive omnicompetent battle hydra build that has no gaps in its defense and has ways to attack effectively in any situation needs so much XP that most games will never see one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-02T07:30:09-07:00","id":1264268,"title":"","content":"While I haven't seen it used much, it does seem to be a style with strengths (getting high damage vs low defence people, defence) and weaknesses (you power it by consuming your own initiative, it's not great vs high defence opponents) and, well... different styles having different strengths and weaknesses seems like good design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-02T07:31:36-07:00","id":1264269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1264261#post1264261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wait what - no, it isn't.<br /> <br /> Cloud of Ebon Devils literally says &amp;quot;whenever the stylist aims with a firewand, she may also reload it&amp;quot;. It specifically says &amp;quot;aims&amp;quot;, rather than &amp;quot;uses his action to aim&amp;quot;. Guess what the Form Charm gives you? Free reflexive aims against characters you've successfully influenced at its activation (or later social actions). This is one of the most basic ways the style's effects combo together, I can't believe that the entire thread missed this.<br /> <br /> Back on topic: the reason why I feel that it's pointless to worry about how easy it is to counter Steel Devil's shtick is that in Ex3, <i>basically any build can be countered</i>. If your GM wants you to have a difficult time, you will have a difficult time. If they want to give you an easy win that plays to your style's strengths, you will get an easy win that plays to your style's strengths. A comprehensive omnicompetent battle hydra build that has no gaps in its defense and has ways to attack effectively in any situation needs so much XP that most games will never see one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention that battle hydra would also need defences against poison clouds, chaos fields and all that other nonsense that isn\u2019t technically combat applicable.<br /> <br /> You\u2019re right about the reflexive aim reload thing too, totally missed that. It will be interesting to see how some of the corebook MAs look in a terrestrial game, especially with the free disappearing 6s. I might have to bring it up to my players and just either make sure they\u2019re all on board, or if they\u2019re not restrict some stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-02T10:47:54-07:00","id":1264298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263386-help-with-steal-devil-ma?p=1264210#post1264210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At worst one can always flurry the reload.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've been toying with a houserule to allow the Quick Draw merit to also apply to reloading, otherwise someone would just grab it and do their best impression of Meryl Strife from Trigun and just have bandoliers of single shot flame pieces that they discard and Quick Draw. Funny for one character/encounter, kinda silly if it is the optimal method outside of charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-05T02:39:44-08:00","id":1264710,"title":"","content":"Steel Devil can be powerful if you can leverage it's 'trick', and work around it's weakness. Stealth and SPSitV elevate it to something really vicious. Better than Ebon Shadow or Thrown in my opinion for assassin type play. <br /> <br /> You open with a strong withering ambush-attack, preferably against what appears to be the squishiest opponent, and chain in Steel Devil Strike (or Empty Mind Strike). If you add SPSitV's Fatal Stroke Flash you are basically making a huge decisive attacks without resetting. Odds are <i>really</i> good you incapacitate your opponent and can use stealth to remain hidden and go for another ambush. Rinse and repeat and see how high you can get your initiative!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}